1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:03,706
Between the seventh and eighth books there's

2
00:00:03,726 --> 00:00:06,481
a short story called Auberon.

3
00:00:06,501 --> 00:00:08,581
Laconia has taken the gates,

4
00:00:08,601 --> 00:00:10,331
and now it has to rule more

5
00:00:10,351 --> 00:00:12,256
than a thousand worlds.

6
00:00:12,276 --> 00:00:14,056
Auberon is one of the richest of

7
00:00:14,076 --> 00:00:16,106
them, and its new governor is about

8
00:00:16,126 --> 00:00:18,356
to learn how hard that job really

9
00:00:18,376 --> 00:00:19,206
is.

10
00:00:19,226 --> 00:00:20,543
Spoilers ahead!

11
00:00:21,278 --> 00:00:23,983
Biryar Rittenaur is a Laconian officer,

12
00:00:24,003 --> 00:00:25,633
and a true believer.

13
00:00:25,653 --> 00:00:27,705
Duarte sends him to govern Auberon,

14
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:30,388
a busy trading world full of ships,

15
00:00:30,408 --> 00:00:32,093
money, and crime.

16
00:00:32,113 --> 00:00:33,443
He brings his wife Mona,

17
00:00:33,463 --> 00:00:35,188
a soil scientist,

18
00:00:35,208 --> 00:00:36,738
and a simple plan:

19
00:00:36,758 --> 00:00:38,338
clean the place up.

20
00:00:38,358 --> 00:00:40,233
No bribes, no smuggling,

21
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:42,398
and Laconian law for everyone.

22
00:00:43,048 --> 00:00:45,578
But Auberon already has its own rulers.

23
00:00:45,598 --> 00:00:48,598
A hidden crime boss runs the docks,

24
00:00:48,618 --> 00:00:50,818
the police, and half the government.

25
00:00:50,848 --> 00:00:53,908
He's Erich, Amos's old boss from Baltimore,

26
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:56,098
a long way from home.

27
00:00:56,153 --> 00:00:58,783
The governor's crackdown goes nowhere.

28
00:00:58,803 --> 00:01:00,853
Erich doesn't fight him head on.

29
00:01:00,878 --> 00:01:02,633
He finds the one thing the governor

30
00:01:02,653 --> 00:01:05,313
can't protect: the woman he loves.

31
00:01:06,044 --> 00:01:06,549
In the end,

32
00:01:06,569 --> 00:01:07,924
the governor keeps his title,

33
00:01:07,944 --> 00:01:10,519
but he rules on Erich's terms.

34
00:01:10,634 --> 00:01:13,664
Laconia's reports say Auberon is calm and

35
00:01:13,684 --> 00:01:14,664
loyal.

36
00:01:14,684 --> 00:01:17,164
Underneath, it runs the way it always

37
00:01:17,184 --> 00:01:18,139
has.

38
00:01:18,159 --> 00:01:20,404
Laconia can conquer a world in a

39
00:01:20,424 --> 00:01:20,964
day.

40
00:01:20,984 --> 00:01:22,905
Ruling one is something else.

41
00:01:23,611 --> 00:01:26,511
That is the crack in Laconia's empire.

42
00:01:26,611 --> 00:01:28,921
Its colonies obey on the surface,

43
00:01:28,941 --> 00:01:31,496
and keep their own rules underneath.

44
00:01:31,516 --> 00:01:33,616
Naomi will remember that.

45
00:01:33,641 --> 00:01:35,221
When she needs a place to rebuild

46
00:01:35,241 --> 00:01:38,196
the resistance, she goes to Auberon.

47
00:01:38,216 --> 00:01:39,921
Next up: book eight,

48
00:01:39,941 --> 00:01:41,356
Tiamat's Wrath.

